From 0a1b4c022fdead0f87e7ea99010dd1e571929821 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 11:37:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "serial: core: Call device_set_awake_path() for
 console port"

This reverts commit a47cf07f60dcb02d01daa19ecf2d5775d6cd12db.

The original patch force the USART's power-domain to be active when
console_suspend is disabled. This is kind of a regression regarding STM32
ecosystem, as if we disable console_suspend, the platform didn't go in the
expected low-power mode. Moreover STM32s are not impacted by the issue
described by the original patch due to the use of proprietary power
domains.

This "regression" exist only on boards that are still using
stm32_pm_domain (drivers/soc/st/stm32_pm_domain.c) power domains
(STM32MP15x and STM32MP13x) and will probably disappears after the next
kernel rebase as stm32_pm_domain power domains are already deprecated.

Please do not upstream this patch.

Change-Id: I2f952ecbc61ed25716f082ccdad72c35f1897787
Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/571974
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
@@ -2354,7 +2354,6 @@ int uart_suspend_port(struct uart_driver
 			guard(uart_port_lock_irq)(uport);
 			uport->ops->stop_rx(uport);
 		}
-		device_set_awake_path(uport->dev);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
